{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:OrganicChemistry.RingClosureBarrier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"OrganicChemistry.RingClosureBarrier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Even","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Common"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.ring_opening_exceeds_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.ring_opening_exceeds_closure","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.lean#L44-L52","doc":"The ring-opening barrier exceeds the ring-closure barrier.\nFormally: the threading link provides additional stabilisation\nequal to the Alexander weight saved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.weight_diff_monotone","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.weight_diff_monotone","kind":"theorem","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.lean#L33-L42","doc":"The weight difference increases with N (for even N ≥ 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.alexander_weight_diff_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.alexander_weight_diff_six","kind":"theorem","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.lean#L28-L31","doc":"For N = 6, the Alexander weight difference is 2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Organic.alexanderWeightDifference","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Organic.alexanderWeightDifference","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.lean#L21-L26","doc":"The Alexander weight difference between chain and threaded ring.\nFor even N: (N-1) - N/2 = (N-2)/2.\nThis quantity is proportional to the energy barrier. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:ring-closure-barrier","label":"conj:ring-closure-barrier","md":"quantum-observable-universe/organic-chemistry/ring-closure-barrier.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}